# Per-service build-context filter (ADR-0101, ADR-0200). BuildKit reads this file
# (next to the Dockerfile) in preference to any root .dockerignore, so each build
# states its own context rules — there is no hidden repo-wide default. A Go service
# image compiles ONLY Go sources (go.mod/go.sum, libs/go, services/*); everything
# else is kept out of the build context. The frontend, which needs apps/ + libs/ts,
# has its own filter (apps/frontend/Dockerfile.dockerignore).
**/.git
**/.DS_Store
**/node_modules

# Non-Go workspaces and assets.
apps/
libs/ts/

# Repo plumbing not needed to compile a service.
docs/
infra/
# …except the funnel definitions, which this image BAKES IN (see the Dockerfile's
# COPY of infra/analytics/funnels.yaml). An exclusion that swallows a file the
# Dockerfile copies does not fail at review or at lint — it fails at build, as
# `failed to compute cache key: failed to calculate checksum`, which names neither
# the file nor this list. Re-include what is needed rather than narrowing `infra/`,
# so a new plumbing directory stays out by default.
!infra/analytics/
scripts/
tools/
.github/

# Root tooling/config not needed to compile a service.
biome.jsonc
package.json
cog.toml
.golangci.yml
.rumdl.toml

# Markdown anywhere (incl. per-service READMEs).
**/*.md
